      "moduleId": "japanese-basics",
      "focus": "Practice polite ～ます forms for familiar actions; a time word such as あした can also make them describe a future action. で marks where an action happens (としょかんで はたらきます); と marks the person you do it with (ともだちと はなします), rather than linking two nouns as in Foundation.",
